From 4660fcdde8650dc5e5020533ca4c12f44f4003bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: batya <batya@github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:59:07 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] feat(library): a track is made inside a session, its
 parts play, and old stems are archived
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Nothing is generated outside a session. The create button asks the service for the active
session first and, when there is none, opens the session dialog while the request waits and
runs right after it is created. The service itself holds the same gate: generation, stems,
karaoke, processing, MIDI transcription and audio import answer 409 while no session is open,
exactly like the agent's own tools. A finished track joins the open session, so what a person
made is where they look for it - before, it was saved in the library behind the session and
the person saw "Track ready" but no track.

A part of a song (a stem) now says what it is doing in the library list: it carries its own
play/pause and state, and its name reads in the person's language (five languages) instead of
the latin stem the service records. Stems keep being told apart by metadata.derived only.

Separating a song again no longer deletes the previous set. The old stems, their files and
the link to the song they were separated from move into the archive (a stems_archive table
plus a stems-archive folder per song and set, labelled СТЕМ-<date time>), and only then the
new set is written. The archive answers on GET /v1/library/stems-archive and through the
stems_archive_list tool.
